# Per-Repository Pull Request Gates

Run the gate locally before pushing and see its exit code. Verified against
each repo's workflow and manifest on 2026-07-27. When a repo's CI and this
table disagree, CI wins and this table is stale — fix it in the same change.

## bran-dev, bran (Rust)

Source: `.github/workflows/bran-fast.yml`, `tools/ci/check.sh`.

```sh
./tools/ci/check.sh --fast     # what CI runs on every PR
./tools/ci/check.sh --full     # before requesting review
```

Modes: `--fast --full --conformance --security --performance --test-budget
--export --tui`. Add `--security` for trust-boundary diffs and `--export` for
anything the public mirror carries. Toolchain is pinned to Rust 1.94.1.

Export and cutover, batched and owner-triggered, never part of merge:
`./tools/ci/check.sh --export`, `tools/ci/public_boundary_check.py`,
`tools/cutover/publish-hygiene.sh`.

## alphazede-markets (Rust + Python)

Source: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.

```sh
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo test --workspace
cargo fmt --workspace --check
pip install -e ".[dev]" && pytest tests/ -m "not integration"
```

## alphazede-sports (pnpm)

Source: `package.json`, `.github/workflows/`, `tools/ci/`.

```sh
pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm test
pnpm test:contracts && pnpm test:ui
pnpm test:e2e            # test:e2e:ci in CI
```

Additional workflow gates: `frontend-spec-gate.yml`, `audit.yml`, `codeql.yml`.
`tools/ci/` holds repo-specific checks (`check-ci-tooling.sh`,
`check-services-source-hygiene.sh`, and others) — run the ones your diff
touches.

## azedge

Source: `.github/workflows/quality.yml`, `package.json`, `tools/ci/`.

```sh
pnpm lint && pnpm test
```

Contract scripts in `tools/ci/`: `foundation-contracts.sh`,
`data-contracts.sh`, `outcome-schema.sh`, `compatibility-equivalence.sh`,
`package-manifests.sh`.

## developers

Source: `.github/workflows/`. Gates: `bran-fast.yml`, `window-verify.yml`,
`codeql.yml`, `semgrep.yml`. Publishing runs through `npm-publish.yml` and
`bran-release.yml`.

## Alphazedehq (umbrella)

Source: `.github/workflows/coe-gates.yml`, the only tracked workflow (CodeQL is
GitHub-managed and has no file here). Its single `coe-gates` job runs on every
pull request and on push to `main`, and runs these commands in order:

```sh
python3 tools/coe/lint-plan-spec.py                 # all of docs/plans, not just the diff
shopt -s globstar                                   # needed for the ** pattern
python3 tools/coe/lint-sdoc.py docs/coe/**/*.sdoc
bash tools/coe/test-pre-commit-gates.sh             # the pre-commit gate's own suite
python3 hooks/test-issue-labels.py
bash hooks/test-bug-report-routing.sh
bash skills/ship-pull-request/tests/edit-pr.test.sh # PR edit tooling & stale-text verification
node --test skills/test-engineering/tests/te-evaluator.test.cjs
python3 skills/test-engineering/tests/te-receipt-contract.test.py
python3 skills/test-engineering/tests/ponytail-on-off.test.py
```

The first three install nothing: two stdlib-only Python linters and a Bash
suite. The three
Test Engineering suites need Node 22 and Python 3.12, and the last two need the
isolated Draft 2020-12 validator. CI provisions that validator into the runner
temp from `tools/coe/te-schema-validator-requirements.txt` with a hash-pinned
`pip install --require-hashes --no-deps --target`, then exports the target
directory as `EMV_SCHEMA_VALIDATOR_IMPORTS`. Running the last two locally means
pointing the same variable at your own verified import directory:

```sh
EMV_SCHEMA_VALIDATOR_IMPORTS=<your verified imports> \
  python3 skills/test-engineering/tests/te-receipt-contract.test.py
```

The validator is a test fixture, never a product dependency: `--target` keeps it
off the interpreter every other step uses, and it is never installed globally.
Its pins are the six SCAN-EMV-SCHEMA-VALIDATOR-001 packages, byte-identical to
Bearing Lite's `test/schema-validator-requirements.txt`; change the two files
together or not at all.

No Test Engineering step is conditional. A missing adapter, schema or suite
fails the job rather than being skipped, so absent product cannot read as a
green gate.

Local-only, and deliberately not run by CI:

```sh
./tools/bran/runtime/bran check . bran-strict    # any docs/ or skills/ change
tools/coe/validate-sdoc.sh                  # any docs/coe/ change; needs AZ_REQUIREMENTS_STRICTDOC_WHEEL
tools/coe/pre-commit-gates.sh               # the two lint gates, over staged paths
```

`coe-gates.yml` runs neither the StrictDoc bridge nor `validate-sdoc.sh`: both
need the packaged engine, which is an installed payload on an owner node and is
not available to a hosted runner. `pre-commit-gates.sh` is tracked but only
active in a checkout whose owner has chained it into `.git/hooks/pre-commit` —
see `hooks/README.md` § The repository gates.

The live plan-record grammar for new work: a Journey writes
`<journey-topic>-technical-plan.md` with frontmatter `type: technical-plan`,
alongside the approved artifact names `design.md`, `seit.json`,
`implementation.json` and `review.html`. `type: plan-spec` stays a valid legacy
input and the historical records keep their names; the command names
`lint-plan-spec.py` and `pre-commit-gates.sh` are unchanged. What
`lint-plan-spec.py` gates is the declared Markdown `type` — the JSON artifact
names are the writing convention, not a gate.

Verify the runtime against `tools/bran/runtime/bran-release-pin.json` before
running it. Documentation-only and skill-only changes use deterministic
self-review per `AGENTS.md` § Code review policy.

## betbot

No CI workflow is present. The gate is the repo's own review flow — see
`betbot/AGENTS.md` and `betbot/CLAUDE.md`, with `scripts/bug_hunter_*.sh` for
the bug-hunter pass. Confirm the intended gate with the owner before merging;
do not invent a command.
