# Pull Request Body Contract

Four sections, in this order. A missing section is a blocked PR.

```markdown
## What changed

- One bullet per externally visible change, imperative mood.
- Name the invariant a change establishes, not the files it touched.

## Why

The property that did not hold before and holds now. State the constraint the
change was built under when one shaped the design.

## Validation

- Each command exactly as run, one per line.
- The result: counts, exit status, what the output showed.

## Residual risk

- Every gate not run, and why.
- Every accepted limitation of the approach.
- `no known gap` only when that is literally true.
```

## Rules

- Validation lists commands actually run in this branch. A command you intend
  to run belongs under Residual risk until it has run.
- An unavailable environment is a residual risk, not an omission. Name the
  missing configuration.
- This body is the permanent review record for the change. Rebase-merge keeps
  the individual commit messages, so the body is not the commit message. Write
  both to be read a year later by someone bisecting.
- When creating or editing PR descriptions, never use `gh pr edit` (on Ubuntu
  `gh 2.45.0`, it fails on the deprecated Projects-classic GraphQL schema and
  silently leaves text stale). Always update using GitHub REST PATCH
  (`gh api -X PATCH repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/<n> -F body=@<file>` or
  `scripts/edit-pr.sh`) and perform the verification
  readback (`gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/<n> --jq '{title: .title, body: .body}'`
  or `scripts/check-pr-text.sh`) to detect and reject stale PR text.

## Worked example

`alphazede/bran-dev#14` states its gate output (`--fast`, 263 core and 38 CLI
tests) and discloses that the live external-host smoke test could not run
because the required environment configuration was unavailable, and that the
PR therefore stays draft. That disclosure is the pattern to copy.
7090d44 feat(setup-a-repo): add checked PR workflow authoring
47c46f2 docs: make verified issue closure routine agent work
30818ca Improve bug triage orchestration and regression prevention
f571ac6 Merge pull request #292 from alphazede/feat/issue-labels-find-update
# AGENTS.md — AlphaZede Workspace Root

`$HOME/alphazede` is a **multi-repo workspace container, not a repository.**
No `.git`, no `.bran/policy.yaml`, no build, no tests, no commits at this level.

This file is canonical for agents that start here. Its only job is to answer two
questions fast: **where am I**, and **which repository does the owner mean?**
Once you know the repo, that repo's own `AGENTS.md` takes over and this file stops
applying.

## Authority order

1. Current owner (William Rumph) instructions in this session
2. The target repository's `AGENTS.md` and any path-specific nested `AGENTS.md`
3. The target repository's `CLAUDE.md` / `AGY.md` / `GEMINI.md` / `QWEN.md` lens
4. This file (workspace routing only)

A rule stated inside a repo always beats a summary written here.

## Orientation tree

```
$HOME/alphazede/
├── alphazede-markets/     AZM — options trading engine        [git: alphazede/btm]
│   ├── btm/               Rust Cargo workspace (5 crates) + Python IBKR bridge
│   ├── btm-fpga/          RTL/HLS Vivado projects, Kria KV260 deployment
│   ├── btm-ibkr/          IBKR integration
│   └── deploy/ docs/ lessons/ prompts/ reports/ tests/ ui/ Vnv/ Xilinx/
├── alphazede-sports/      AZS — fantasy + sports betting      [git: alphazede/alphazede-sports]
│   ├── command_node/ data_node/ services/  distributed runtime
│   ├── apps/ frontend/ packages/           Next.js / TypeScript
│   ├── hardware/ infra/ deploy/            FPGA + fleet
│   └── agents/ docs/ tools/ tests/ Vnv/ Security/
├── betbot/                BTO — legacy production sports bot  [git: 1wgrumph/betbot]
│   └── analysis/ core/ engines/ models/ pipeline/ clients/ docs/ tests/
├── azedge/                AZEdge foundation (Rust + pnpm)     [local only]
